<title>BELGIUM: Key figures from OECD survey on Belgium.</title>
<headline>Key figures from OECD survey on Belgium.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of key forecasts for Belgium released by Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development (OECD) on Tuesday. (all figures in percent)</p>
<p>					   1996	1997     1998</p>
<p>    Real GDP			    1.3	 2.2	2.6</p>
<p>    Deficit/GDP			 3.2	 2.9	2.7</p>
<p>    Debt/GDP			  129.9     127.2    124.6</p>
<p>    GDP price deflator		1.6	 2.0	1.7</p>
<p>    Inflation			   2.0	 1.9	1.7</p>
<p>    Short-term interest rates     3.2	 3.1	3.7</p>
<p>    Long-term interest rates	6.4	 6.2	6.4</p>
<p>NOTE - The OECD said its survey was based on the annual review of Belgium's economy carried out in January. It noted its previous country report on Belgium was published in September 1995.</p>
<p>* Full report (includes Luxembourg) costs 125 French francs. Available from OECD Publications, 2 Rue Andre-Pascal, 75775 Paris, France.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
